messages.reasoning_content:
The existing readiness probe is explicitly checking `/readyz`. Since the image is Nginx, this endpoint does not exist, causing 404 errors and eventually connection refusal (or perceived failure by kubelet).

I will patch the Deployment to change the readiness probe path from `/readyz` to `/`.

Patch specification:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "readinessProbe": {
              "httpGet": {
                "path": "/",
                "port": 80
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
I will apply this patch using `kubectl patch`.
Note: I need to ensure I specify the correct container name, which I observed as `app` in the pod description.

